/-!
# The punctured spectrum of a reduction is a thickening of the punctured spectrum

Let `A` be a commutative ring and `I ⊆ A` an ideal consisting of nilpotent elements, so that the
closed immersion `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A` is a homeomorphism on points: a thickening.  This file
carries that thickening over to the punctured spectra `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` and
`U' = Spec(A / I) ∖ V(𝔞 (A / I))`, and over to the closed subschemes of those opens cut out by an
ideal `J ⊆ A` and by its image.

The upshot is the data that the transport of full faithfulness along a thickening consumes: a
thickening `U' ⟶ U` of ambient schemes, a thickening of closed subschemes lying over it, and the
square relating the two.  For `I` the nilradical this is the step "replace `A` by its reduction"
in the study of finite étale covers of a punctured spectrum, which is what makes a dimension
hypothesis on the minimal primes of `A` usable: the associated primes of a reduced ring are its
minimal primes.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.complementZeroLocusQuotientMap` — the induced morphism `U' ⟶ U` of
  punctured spectra.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap` — the induced morphism of the
  closed subschemes of `U'` and `U` cut out by the image of `J` and by `J`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isThickening_specMap_quotientMk` — `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A` is a
  thickening as soon as `I` consists of nilpotents.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isThickening_complementZeroLocusQuotientMap` — so is the induced
  morphism `U' ⟶ U` of punctured spectra.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isThickening_subschemeMap` — a thickening of ambient schemes induces a
  thickening of closed subschemes, once the ideal sheaf downstairs is contained in the pushforward
  of the one upstairs and the supports match.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.comap_idealSheafNearVanishing` — the ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on `U'` is the
  inverse image of the ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on `U`.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isThickening_idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap` — the closed subscheme
  of `U'` cut out by the image of `J` is a thickening of the closed subscheme of `U` cut out
  by `J`.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.finiteEtaleColimitFullyFaithful_of_completionComplete_nilradical` —
  full faithfulness of `colim_V FÉt_V ⟶ FÉt_{V(f) ∩ U}` follows from full faithfulness of the
  completion functor near the corresponding closed subscheme of the punctured spectrum of the
  reduction of `A`.

## Implementation notes

The punctured spectrum of `A / I` is not literally the inverse image along `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A`
of the punctured spectrum of `A`; the two opens are equal, by
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preimage_complementZeroLocus_specMap_quotientMk`, and the morphism of
punctured spectra is the restriction of `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A` precomposed with the isomorphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isoOfEq` attached to that equality.

The ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on a punctured spectrum is generated by global sections, so the
comparison of the two ideal sheaves is a statement about ideals of global sections: by
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_ofIdealTop` the inverse image of the ideal sheaf generated by an ideal
of global sections is generated by the image of that ideal, and the map on global functions of
`U' ⟶ U` carries the generators coming from `J` to those coming from the image of `J`.

Both the ideal `J` of `A` and the ideal of `A / I` cutting out the subscheme of `U'` are left as
arguments, related by an equality hypothesis, so that the statements apply to the two spellings
`(J)(A / I)` and `(J mod I)` of the image of a principal ideal without a transport of the
subscheme along an equality of ideals.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Stacks.Thickenings Stacks.LocalCohomology

universe u

namespace Stacks.FundamentalGroup

/-! ### The spectrum of a quotient by nilpotents -/

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-- **The spectrum of a quotient by an ideal of nilpotents is a thickening.**  The quotient map
is surjective, so the morphism of spectra is a closed immersion, and the image of a prime of
`A / I` is a prime of `A` containing `I`; since every prime of `A` contains the nilradical, every
prime of `A` arises this way. -/
@[ega "I 1.1.12" "more general"]
theorem isThickening_specMap_quotientMk (hI : I ≤ nilradical A) :
    IsThickening (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) := by
  refine ⟨IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective, fun x => ?_⟩
  have hrange : Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) = Set.univ := by
    rw [range_comap_of_surjective _ _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective, Ideal.mk_ker]
    refine Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset ?_
    rw [← PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_nilradical]
    exact PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_anti_mono_ideal hI
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : x ∈ Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :=
    hrange ▸ Set.mem_univ x
  exact ⟨y, hy⟩

/-- **The punctured spectrum of a quotient is the inverse image of the punctured spectrum.**  The
inverse image of the complement of `V(𝔞)` is the complement of the zero locus of the image of
`𝔞`. -/
theorem preimage_complementZeroLocus_specMap_quotientMk (a : Ideal A) :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) ⁻¹ᵁ complementZeroLocus A a =
      complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) := by
  apply TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext
  change PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) ⁻¹'
      (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (a : Set A))ᶜ =
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus ((a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) : Ideal (A ⧸ I)) : Set (A ⧸ I)))ᶜ
  rw [Set.preimage_compl, PrimeSpectrum.preimage_comap_zeroLocus, Ideal.map,
    PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_span]

/-! ### The induced morphism of punctured spectra -/

variable (a : Ideal A)

/-- The morphism `Spec(A / I) ∖ V(𝔞 (A / I)) ⟶ Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` of punctured spectra induced by
the quotient map `A ⟶ A / I`: the restriction of `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A` over `Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`,
read through the identification of the inverse image of `Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` with
`Spec(A / I) ∖ V(𝔞 (A / I))`. -/
def complementZeroLocusQuotientMap :
    (complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) : Scheme.{u}) ⟶
      (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme.{u}) :=
  ((Spec (CommRingCat.of (A ⧸ I))).isoOfEq
      (preimage_complementZeroLocus_specMap_quotientMk A I a)).inv ≫
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) ∣_ complementZeroLocus A a)

/-- The morphism of punctured spectra lies over the morphism of spectra. -/
theorem complementZeroLocusQuotientMap_ι :
    complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a ≫ (complementZeroLocus A a).ι =
      (complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).ι ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) := by
  rw [complementZeroLocusQuotientMap, Category.assoc, morphismRestrict_ι, ← Category.assoc,
    Scheme.isoOfEq_inv_ι]

/-- **The punctured spectrum of a quotient by nilpotents is a thickening of the punctured
spectrum.**  A thickening restricts to a thickening over an open of the ambient scheme, and an
isomorphism is a thickening. -/
theorem isThickening_complementZeroLocusQuotientMap (hI : I ≤ nilradical A) :
    IsThickening (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a) :=
  isThickening_comp (isThickening_of_isIso _)
    ((isThickening_specMap_quotientMk A I hI).morphismRestrict _)

/-! ### A thickening of ambient schemes thickens the closed subschemes -/

/-- **A thickening of ambient schemes induces a thickening of closed subschemes.**  Let
`i : X' ⟶ X` be a thickening and let `Y ⊆ X` and `Y' ⊆ X'` be closed subschemes with `Y` contained
in the pushforward of `Y'`, so that `i` restricts to a morphism `Y' ⟶ Y`.  If the inverse image of
the support of `Y` is contained in the support of `Y'`, then `Y' ⟶ Y` is again a thickening.

The restricted morphism is a closed immersion because its composite with the closed immersion of
`Y` is one, namely the composite of the closed immersions of `Y'` and `i`.  It is surjective
because a point of `Y` is the image of a point of `X'`, which then lies in the support of `Y'` and
so comes from a point of `Y'`. -/
theorem isThickening_subschemeMap {X X' : Scheme.{u}} {i : X' ⟶ X} (hi : IsThickening i)
    (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (Y' : X'.IdealSheafData) (H : Y ≤ Y'.map i)
    (hsupp : i.base ⁻¹' (Y.support : Set X) ⊆ (Y'.support : Set X')) :
    IsThickening (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap Y' Y i H) := by
  have := hi.1
  have hsq := Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι Y' Y i H
  refine ⟨?_, fun y => ?_⟩
  · have : IsClosedImmersion (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap Y' Y i H ≫ Y.subschemeι) := by
      rw [hsq]; infer_instance
    exact IsClosedImmersion.of_comp_isClosedImmersion _ Y.subschemeι
  · have hy : Y.subschemeι y ∈ (Y.support : Set X) := by
      rw [← Y.range_subschemeι]; exact ⟨y, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hi.2 (Y.subschemeι y)
    have hx' : x ∈ (Y'.support : Set X') := hsupp (by rw [Set.mem_preimage, hx]; exact hy)
    rw [← Y'.range_subschemeι] at hx'
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx'
    refine ⟨z, Y.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.injective ?_⟩
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hsq, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hx]

/-! ### The closed subscheme cut out by an ideal of the base ring -/

variable (J : Ideal A) (K : Ideal (A ⧸ I))

/-- **The morphism of punctured spectra carries the ideal generated by `J` to the ideal generated
by the image of `J`.**  The morphism of punctured spectra lies over `Spec(A / I) ⟶ Spec A`, whose
map on global functions is the quotient map read through the identification of `Γ(Spec R, 𝒪)` with
`R`. -/
theorem map_appTop_baseIdeal_complementZeroLocus :
    Ideal.map (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a).appTop.hom
        (Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal A J (complementZeroLocus A a).ι)
      = Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdeal (A ⧸ I) (J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
          (complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).ι := by
  have hhom : ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv ≫
        (complementZeroLocus A a).ι.appTop) ≫ (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a).appTop
      = CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) ≫
        ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (A ⧸ I))).inv ≫
          (complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).ι.appTop) := by
    rw [Category.assoc, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, complementZeroLocusQuotientMap_ι,
      Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, ← Category.assoc, ← Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality, Category.assoc]
  change Ideal.map (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a).appTop.hom
      (Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv ≫
        (complementZeroLocus A a).ι.appTop).hom J) = _
  rw [Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, hhom, CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← Ideal.map_map,
    CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
  rfl

/-- **The ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on the punctured spectrum of `A / I` is the inverse image of the
ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on the punctured spectrum of `A`.**  Both are generated by global sections,
and the morphism of punctured spectra carries the generators of one to the generators of the
other. -/
theorem comap_idealSheafNearVanishing (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A J a).comap
        (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a)
      = Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ I) K
          (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) := by
  subst hK
  unfold Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing
  unfold Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.baseIdealSheaf
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_ofIdealTop, map_appTop_baseIdeal_complementZeroLocus]

/-- **The ideal sheaf `J · 𝒪` on the punctured spectrum is contained in the pushforward of the
ideal sheaf generated by the image of `J`.** -/
theorem idealSheafNearVanishing_le_map (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A J a ≤
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ I) K
          (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).map (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a) :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le.mpr
    (comap_idealSheafNearVanishing A I a J K hK).le

/-- **The support of the ideal sheaf generated by the image of `J` is the inverse image of the
support of `J · 𝒪`.** -/
theorem preimage_support_idealSheafNearVanishing (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a).base ⁻¹'
        ((Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A J a).support :
          Set (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme.{u}))
      = ((Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ I) K
          (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).support :
        Set (complementZeroLocus (A ⧸ I) (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) : Scheme.{u})) := by
  rw [← comap_idealSheafNearVanishing A I a J K hK, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap,
    TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_preimage]

/-- The morphism of closed subschemes of the punctured spectra cut out by `J` and by the image of
`J`, the restriction of the morphism of punctured spectra. -/
def idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ I) K
        (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).subscheme ⟶
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A J a).subscheme :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap _ _ (complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a)
    (idealSheafNearVanishing_le_map A I a J K hK)

/-- The morphism of closed subschemes lies over the morphism of punctured spectra. -/
theorem idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap_subschemeι (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap A I a J K hK ≫
        (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A J a).subschemeι =
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ I) K
          (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))).subschemeι ≫ complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι _ _ _ _

/-- **The closed subscheme of the punctured spectrum of `A / I` cut out by the image of `J` is a
thickening of the closed subscheme of the punctured spectrum of `A` cut out by `J`.** -/
theorem isThickening_idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap (hI : I ≤ nilradical A)
    (hK : K = J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    IsThickening (idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap A I a J K hK) :=
  isThickening_subschemeMap (isThickening_complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A I a hI) _ _ _
    (preimage_support_idealSheafNearVanishing A I a J K hK).le

/-- The image of a principal ideal under the quotient map is the principal ideal on the image of
the generator. -/
theorem map_span_singleton_quotient (f : A) :
    (Ideal.span {f}).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) = Ideal.span {Ideal.Quotient.mk I f} := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

/-! ### Descent of full faithfulness from the reduction -/

/-- **Full faithfulness of the restriction functor on finite étale covers near `V(f)` in a
punctured spectrum descends from the reduction.**  Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `𝔞 ⊆ A` an ideal,
`f ∈ A`, and write `A_red = A / nil(A)`.  If the completion functor on coherent modules is fully
faithful near the closed subscheme of the punctured spectrum of `A_red` cut out by the image of
`f`, then the restriction functor
`colim_{V} FÉt_V ⟶ FÉt_{V(f) ∩ (Spec A ∖ V(𝔞))}` is fully faithful.

The reduction of `A` has the same punctured spectrum as `A` up to a thickening, and the closed
subschemes cut out by `f` and by its image correspond under it, so this is the transport of full
faithfulness along a thickening.  It is the step "replace `A` by its reduction" in the study of
finite étale covers of a punctured spectrum, which is what makes a dimension hypothesis on the
minimal primes of `A` usable: the associated primes of a reduced ring are its minimal primes. -/
theorem finiteEtaleColimitFullyFaithful_of_completionComplete_nilradical [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (f : A)
    (h : Stacks.Algebraization.NeighbourhoodCompletion.CompletionFullyFaithfulComplete
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing (A ⧸ nilradical A)
          (Ideal.span {Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical A) f})
          (a.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical A)))).subschemeι) :
    FiniteEtaleColimitFullyFaithful (complementZeroLocus A a : Scheme.{u})
      (Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing A (Ideal.span {f}) a) :=
  have hK := (map_span_singleton_quotient A (nilradical A) f).symm
  finiteEtaleColimitFullyFaithful_of_completionComplete_of_isThickening
    (isThickening_complementZeroLocusQuotientMap A (nilradical A) a le_rfl) _ _ _
    (idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap_subschemeι A (nilradical A) a (Ideal.span {f})
      (Ideal.span {Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical A) f}) hK)
    (isThickening_idealSheafNearVanishingQuotientMap A (nilradical A) a (Ideal.span {f})
      (Ideal.span {Ideal.Quotient.mk (nilradical A) f}) le_rfl hK) h

end Stacks.FundamentalGroup

end
